  "question": {
    "text": "A straight line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> through the point <math><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is inclined at an angle of <math><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> to the line <math><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> also intersects the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis, then the equation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "luMmi",
      "text": "<math><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi> </mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cohei",
      "text": "<math><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi> </mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
